I've left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would reach for authority the graph hasn't granted, and the host would refuse the import at link time. To add the fetch, the platform team would first need to extend the node's declared `with` clause in the graph, for example to `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>`, so the validator and host bind it.

There is also a second problem: `PublishedDigest` has no text field to put in `?q=`. Since the node's output must not change anyway, the body below records the digest's considered items and nothing else.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Only mark items seen once the digest actually went out; an
        // unpublished run leaves them eligible for the next one.
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            let mut done: Vec<&str> = Vec::new();
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                let id = id.as_str();
                if id.is_empty() || done.contains(&id) {
                    continue;
                }
                done.push(id);
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

